  "content": {
    "id": "p22-q15-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "Determine the values of $p$, $q$ and $r$ so that $3x^2-2x-5=px^2+q(x-1)^2+r(x-2)^2$ for all values of $x$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$p=-1$, $q=7$, $r=-3$.",
      "worked": "Expanding the right-hand side gives\n$$\\begin{align*}px^2+q(x-1)^2+r(x-2)^2&=px^2+q(x^2-2x+1)+r(x^2-4x+4)\\\\px^2+q(x-1)^2+r(x-2)^2&=(p+q+r)x^2+(-2q-4r)x+q+4r.\\end{align*}$$\nEquating coefficients gives $p+q+r=3$, $-2q-4r=-2$ and $q+4r=-5$.\n$$\\begin{align*}q+2r&=1\\\\(q+4r)-(q+2r)&=-5-1\\\\2r&=-6\\\\r&=-3\\\\q&=1-2(-3)\\\\q&=7\\\\p&=3-7-(-3)\\\\p&=-1.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 64
  },
